[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64593"] :question/problem "A particle of mass $2\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. The spring constant associated with the spring is $k=18\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.$  The particle is also subject to a resistive force that's proportional to the particle's speed, and has a damping coefficient $c=10\\,\\text{kg/s}.$  The position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in seconds.  If the particle moves with damped harmonic motion, what is the governing equation?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of damped harmonic motion is\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-c{y}^{′}-ky.\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $m,$ $k$ and $c$ gives\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}=-10{y}^{′}-18y.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above equation, we get:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+9y=0\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64617"] :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+7y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical damping.\n- ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+8y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping.\n- ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping." :question/worked-solution "Remember that, given the equation of a damped harmonic oscillator, the type of damping depends on the discriminant of the characteristic equation:\n\n- $D>0$ leads to heavy damping,\n\n- $D=0$ leads to critical damping, and\n\n- $D<0$ leads to light damping.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each equation.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+7y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +7=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={3}^{2}-4(1)(7) & =-19<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents light damping, and so statement I is false.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+8y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +8=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={6}^{2}-4(1)(8) & =4>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents heavy damping, and so statement II is correct.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={8}^{2}-4(1)(16) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents critical damping, and so statement III is false.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-94311/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "57dd3934-9bc5-54e5-9f11-0a86ef953b84" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94311/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "025f9c8c-b92a-5b9d-9560-12d7e07a2303" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94311/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "305573ba-78aa-5688-a91d-84af92c44465" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94311/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" :answer/id #uuid "c873a378-3273-5881-aef0-5637501c5e8e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94311/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "1bcb1a67-db67-56b6-8cf2-26895aa25d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94311/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aeb208b6-24cb-5f43-8985-2eaf15597945" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94311/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" :answer-field/choices ["q-94311/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-94311/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-94311/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-94311/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" "q-94311/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94311" :question/id #uuid "8a56fdf8-4093-582a-8eb3-1fa47565653f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94311" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+2y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping\n- ${y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+7y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping\n- ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical  damping" :question/worked-solution "Remember that, given the equation of a damped harmonic oscillator, the type of damping depends on the discriminant of the characteristic equation:\n\n- $D>0$ leads to heavy damping,\n\n- $D=0$ leads to critical damping, and\n\n- $D<0$ leads to light damping.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each equation.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+2y$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +2=0.\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={6}^{2}-4(1)(2) & =28>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents heavy damping, and so statement I is true.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+7y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda +7=0.\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={5}^{2}-4(1)(7) & =-3<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents light damping, and so statement II is true.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16=0.\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={8}^{2}-4(1)(16) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents critical damping, and so statement III is true.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94311/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "089c1139-6e3a-5240-be03-fb7e54ecbd7c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94311"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94324/selection/ea2ff8a2e75ef8a56533b74c3025d6e61969fb8dc0aa527ae6dd6bc6ff033a41" :answer/id #uuid "d50b4733-17ac-5392-8969-541607d84e2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+2y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94324/selection/6d0b235488392e0a31c79cd510c567e8335554ddc521ad18a479cdd44144e021" :answer/id #uuid "66496ea1-f2ed-50f4-9655-d1e677ef861e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+2y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94324/selection/4b0a0434eb83b667a281d39f6064cddb895a77134d9bb527bab568716428b54e" :answer/id #uuid "bd81993a-d79b-58f4-854a-4c5ee4f579cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+7y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94324/selection/a420bbfb1f1a2605ed93dc1e61ee63f86279d20826dd43b260e31e8c9d82ffc6" :answer/id #uuid "0028312c-8e4d-5205-ba25-90628198a2c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+2y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94324/selection/e2ce6e9f7430c3fff6fc71e626bf7236dcbe779aa6e1413078fa419697be6e77" :answer/id #uuid "61ba141d-e63e-57e2-b6db-32f25c1bafa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94324/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bcb6d120-f8d3-5599-84ed-12974816e9c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94324/selection/a420bbfb1f1a2605ed93dc1e61ee63f86279d20826dd43b260e31e8c9d82ffc6" :answer-field/choices ["q-94324/selection/ea2ff8a2e75ef8a56533b74c3025d6e61969fb8dc0aa527ae6dd6bc6ff033a41" "q-94324/selection/6d0b235488392e0a31c79cd510c567e8335554ddc521ad18a479cdd44144e021" "q-94324/selection/4b0a0434eb83b667a281d39f6064cddb895a77134d9bb527bab568716428b54e" "q-94324/selection/a420bbfb1f1a2605ed93dc1e61ee63f86279d20826dd43b260e31e8c9d82ffc6" "q-94324/selection/e2ce6e9f7430c3fff6fc71e626bf7236dcbe779aa6e1413078fa419697be6e77"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94324" :question/id #uuid "704b1e51-f6aa-5eaa-825a-515f3e83eae5" :question/math-academy-id "q-94324" :question/problem "A particle of mass $14\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. The spring constant associated with the spring is $k=28\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.$  The particle is also subject to a resistive force that's proportional to the particle's velocity, and has a damping coefficient $c=14\\,\\text{kg/s}.$  The position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in seconds.  If the particle moves with damped harmonic motion, what is the governing equation?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of damped harmonic motion is\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-c{y}^{′}-ky.\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $m,$ $k$ and $c$ gives\n\n$$\n14{y}^{″}=-14{y}^{′}-28y.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+2y=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94324/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfa8f9b2-1628-5f9f-8f0e-0fd6c01c70d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94324"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94359/selection/c52fa96f46dc62b1281c92c37627774fac8b92062bf7f987f12de62459a56846" :answer/id #uuid "244ca7a2-2043-5ae4-929c-f91939d47b52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi \\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94359/selection/3e311265a6bcd67f92fccbb5db03f7bbbf0b2a6e30b3d18363d2686e030dbf15" :answer/id #uuid "0dd8fadb-cc4a-552f-8ebd-de912e53958a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94359/selection/171af590bfaa6921104509a8319b51091a88806b3c82b8e596909a536431bacc" :answer/id #uuid "23a754ea-72be-5685-acda-795d9b8347ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94359/selection/fa390f0fe3bdefe27437e709b214a7a294db52a9b1efe1868e91488b62415aa9" :answer/id #uuid "feb062c5-a381-5673-820c-b0d292620888" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94359/selection/a690dcfd520d09d276d2ba9ed3722b8071bc5f5804cf35b34d123ef2db600227" :answer/id #uuid "254df75f-d9bf-5c29-a12d-8dfbfb4b2295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94359/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "66c128aa-89eb-5e48-95d3-7e6238a342dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94359/selection/c52fa96f46dc62b1281c92c37627774fac8b92062bf7f987f12de62459a56846" :answer-field/choices ["q-94359/selection/c52fa96f46dc62b1281c92c37627774fac8b92062bf7f987f12de62459a56846" "q-94359/selection/3e311265a6bcd67f92fccbb5db03f7bbbf0b2a6e30b3d18363d2686e030dbf15" "q-94359/selection/171af590bfaa6921104509a8319b51091a88806b3c82b8e596909a536431bacc" "q-94359/selection/fa390f0fe3bdefe27437e709b214a7a294db52a9b1efe1868e91488b62415aa9" "q-94359/selection/a690dcfd520d09d276d2ba9ed3722b8071bc5f5804cf35b34d123ef2db600227"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94359" :question/id #uuid "2923e945-2143-52cb-b5fe-a0a714d9e55e" :question/math-academy-id "q-94359" :question/problem "The position $y(t)$ of a particle oscillating with light damped harmonic motion is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+10y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the damped oscillation?" :question/worked-solution "The given equation represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. We are looking for solutions of the form $y={e}^{\\lambda t}.$\n\nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +10=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +10 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9)-9+10 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda +3 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-3\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}={e}^{-3t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡t).\n$$\n\nFrom the solution, the value of the angular frequency is $Ω=1\\,{\\text{s}}^{-1}.$\n\nThe period of the damped oscillation $T$ is related to the angular frequency as follows:\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{Ω}\n$$\n\nSo the period is\n\n$$\nT=2\\pi \\,\\text{s}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94359/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48a64312-22d5-57ed-b83b-254aff2ca870"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94359"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
